---
const signals = [
  {
    stat: '73%',
    label: 'of small businesses now sell across at least two channels.',
    context: 'Up from 38% five years ago. The move to multi-channel is not a trend. It is the baseline.',
  },
  {
    stat: '3× faster',
    label: 'growth for businesses that operate on digital infrastructure vs those that do not.',
    context: 'The gap compounds. Businesses that digitalise early pull ahead. The ones that do not become price-sensitive accounts.',
  },
  {
    stat: 'Right now',
    label: 'Shopify, Square, and a dozen category-specific platforms are actively recruiting your members.',
    context: 'With no-code setup, zero upfront cost, and aggressive onboarding. They are building your network into their platform.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section pb-why-now fade-in" aria-labelledby="pb-why-now-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header center">
      <span class="section-label pb-network-label">Why Now</span>
      <h2 class="headline-lg" id="pb-why-now-title">
        Your members are already digitising.<br />
        <span class="pb-headline-accent">The only question is with who.</span>
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="pb-why-now-body">

      <div class="pb-why-now-signals">
        {signals.map((s) => (
          <div class="pb-signal-card">
            <div class="pb-signal-stat">{s.stat}</div>
            <div class="pb-signal-content">
              <p class="pb-signal-label">{s.label}</p>
              <p class="pb-signal-context">{s.context}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="pb-why-now-argument">
        <div class="pb-argument-block">
          <h3>What is happening right now, in your sector</h3>
          <p>
            Your members are not waiting for permission to go digital. They are onboarding tools, signing
            up for platforms, and figuring it out themselves — because the pressure to sell online, accept
            card payments, and manage orders digitally has become unavoidable.
          </p>
          <p>
            Some of them are doing it well. Most of them are doing it expensively, inefficiently, and on
            someone else's platform. A platform that has no relationship with you. A platform that is
            quietly becoming their most important operational dependency.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pb-argument-block">
          <h3>What happens if you wait</h3>
          <ul class="pb-wait-list">
            <li>
              <span class="pb-wait-icon" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              <span>Your members build operational dependencies on other platforms. Those platforms become harder to displace every month.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="pb-wait-icon" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              <span>The first competitor in your sector who does this owns the digital layer of your market. You become a supplier to their ecosystem.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="pb-wait-icon" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              <span>Your most growth-oriented members — the ones who will shape the next decade — platform themselves independently. Without you.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="pb-wait-icon" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              <span>Every month of inaction is data, transactions, and loyalty accruing to someone else's network.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <blockquote class="pb-why-now-quote">
          Not deciding is also a decision.<br />
          And in this market, the most dangerous one.
        </blockquote>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
